From: Vitrine
Subject: [PATCH] ui/sdl2: QEMU_SDL_POLL_FOCUSED=0 turns the focused polling off

QEMU_SDL_POLL_FOCUSED turned the polling at the refresh rate on whenever
it was set, whatever its value, where QEMU_SDL_ZERO_COPY and
QEMU_SDL_ZC_TILED take 0 for off. Vitrine sets it to 1 for the SDL
window, and a VM's "#env QEMU_SDL_POLL_FOCUSED=0", which the command line
it shows and logs then holds, left the polling on: no #env line can unset
a variable. Vitrine's own patch, for the qemu-gui series to take over.
---
 ui/sdl2.c | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/ui/sdl2.c b/ui/sdl2.c
--- a/ui/sdl2.c
+++ b/ui/sdl2.c
@@ -1562,7 +1562,9 @@ static void sdl2_set_hint_x11_force_egl(void)

 static void sdl2_display_init(DisplayState *ds, DisplayOptions *o)
 {
-    sdl2_poll_focused = getenv("QEMU_SDL_POLL_FOCUSED") != NULL;
+    /* 0 is off, as for QEMU_SDL_ZERO_COPY */
+    sdl2_poll_focused = getenv("QEMU_SDL_POLL_FOCUSED") &&
+                        strcmp(getenv("QEMU_SDL_POLL_FOCUSED"), "0");
     uint8_t data = 0;
     int i;
     SDL_SysWMinfo info;
